tes and and  the like the most depressing part of all  of this for me is that this stuff works  right if the landscape that we had were  one where disinformation didn't spread  wasn't effective we really wouldn't have  to worry about  this so much but this stuff works we've  got anti-vaxxers people who deny climate  change we have people who believe the  most outrageous things and fall for the  silliest disinformation yes they exist  more on the right but this stuff  actually matters and it impacts the left  and we've got to stay on top of it one  of the days sponsors is privacy dot-com  / Pakman which is a free service that I  myself use really useful in many  different ways takes just a few seconds  to link your debit card to privacy com  then you can create virtual credit cards  that are linked directly to your bank  account and you use those virtual credit  card numbers to buy things online which  protects your actual debit card so that  it's not spread all over the internet  and one of the best things about it is  how their mobile app and browser  extensions for Chrome and Firefox make  it really easy to use let's say for  example that I'm signing up for a David  Pakman show membership in the credit  card number field I already see the  privacy com icon I just click it choose  which of my virtual credit cards I want  to use and the credit card number  expiration date and security code are  automatically entered I can put in any  zip code I want and I'm done and if you  try to use my credit card number that  you just saw on the screen it doesn't  matter because I've already deleted that  virtual card and that's the beauty of  privacy calm there are a ton of  advantages to using a free service like  this for example you can sign up for as  many free trials as you want then just  delete the virtual credit card you used  and never worry about getting charged  for it it protects you from getting  hacked it protects you when companies  are hacked which happens all th